{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, this thing just froze again. Uh. You're in about the spot on your back, yeah?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. There's a mole back there and it bled. I'm tired, so can we not make a whole production out of it.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I'm his wife. I booked it because the color changed.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): I can't see the thing. I just woke up with blood on the sheet one time.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): Blood on the sheet. Say that part again? When was that?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Once. About three weeks ago. Then it stopped. And I feel like a wet rag, so let's move.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): It used to be plain light brown. Now there are black patches in it. I noticed maybe a couple of months back.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): It didn't change color. You're looking at it in the bathroom light.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Hold on, the screen jumped. Okay. Partner says the color changed, you say it didn't. Any itching on it?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Does it hurt?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Not really.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): You've got high blood pressure on the chart. Still a thing?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. For years. That's not why I dragged myself in.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Nurse put in the med rec this morning. It says lisinipril twenty milligrams by mouth every morning for the pressure. That what you take?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): Ten milligrams. Once a day. Not twenty. Whoever typed that wasn't in the room.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): The bottle at home says twenty milligrams. I think you've been breaking them in half.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't break them. It's ten. Ugh, I already said it.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, one more time, the dose? I've got three pop-ups.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Ten. Milligrams. Every morning.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): Alright, I'm not picking a winner on the dose. Headaches with the blood pressure?",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): No... well, sometimes. Back of my head.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Dizziness?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Not that either.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Chest pain?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): Never.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): How long's that mole been sitting there?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Five-ish years. I don't know the month. Can you just look?",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): Five years, you said? Left upper back, I can see it from here. Err, let me get the lamp, the cursor just vanished.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Five-ish. Not an exact date. And that waiting room tv was so loud I can't hear myself think, which didn't help.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Tell him about the burns.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): I fried every summer as a kid, blisters and all. Did roofs for twenty years. I've overdone it. Obviously.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): Yeah, a lot of sun. Any rash or other spots anywhere else on the skin?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any drug allergies?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Nothing.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): Mm. Okay, looking, uneven shape, border's notched, brown and black mixed together, about eight millimeters across. Not bleeding right now. Little dry scale on the edge.",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): So what is it. Don't dance around it.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): I can't pin it from the office. Could be an atypical mole, or it could be a melanoma. The color your wife saw, the one time it bled, all that sun, and the way it looks.",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): Fantastic.",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'm putting in a dermatology referral today. They should get you in within two weeks. Don't pick at it. Hat and sunscreen when you're outside.",
  "[SEG0042] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): And if they can't fit him in?",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (DOCTOR): If dermatology cannot see you within two weeks, come back and see me and I'll push them.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): Fine. We done?",
  "[SEG0045] person_1 (DOCTOR): Nurse's sheet from this morning, blood pressure one forty two over eighty eight, pulse seventy six. That's today's.",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): Whatever. Long as I can sit down somewhere.",
  "[SEG0047] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): We'll do the sunscreen. He'll complain the whole time.",
  "[SEG0048] person_1 (DOCTOR): Referral's going in now. Watch the spot till derm sees it."
 ],
